# Subconscious Work

Subconscious Work describes how the mind continues processing problems unconsciously after conscious effort has stalled. Polya notes that incubation—stepping away from a problem and letting it simmer in the background—can lead to breakthroughs. This phenomenon connects to the concept of bright ideas and insights that emerge seemingly from nowhere.

This idea aligns with modern understanding of incubation in cognitive science, where unconscious processing helps reorganize information and generate novel connections. Polya's advice to know when to stop includes recognizing when stepping away from a problem is more productive than continuing to struggle.
